# Now your question might be, Why we use "microsoft defender for cloud" and Why we need to set up security alerts for any type of incident in azure subscription level.


# So lets first understand the use case of "microsoft defender for cloud":

So, "microsoft defender for cloud" service helps you to identify, prevent, and respond to security risks across your resources in Microsoft Azure.

it does:

Security posture management (CSPM)

Finds misconfigurations (e.g., open ports, weak settings)

Threat protection (CWPP)

Detects real attacks like:
Brute-force login attempts
Malware activity
Suspicious network traffic
Recommendations

Tells you what to fix and how to improve security
Compliance tracking

Helps meet standards like ISO, PCI, etc.


And Why we need to set up security alerts for incident?

Team, Defender can detect issues—but alerts are how you know something is wrong in real time.

Without alerts:

Issues stay unnoticed
You only see problems when you manually check
Response is delayed → higher risk

With alerts:

You get instant notification when something happens
You can respond quickly before damage increases
Why alerts for incidents are important

Security incidents can happen anytime, like:

Unauthorized access attempts
Data exfiltration
Suspicious activity on VMs or apps

Alerts help you:
Detect early
Respond faster
Minimize impact
