# Lets understand about Tenant, Management group and subscription.

Tenant (Microsoft Entra ID):
So on the top, we have a Tenant. This is the top-level container. It represents your organization’s identity boundary (users, apps, authentication). You typically have one tenant per organization.

Management Group:
This sits inside a tenant. It’s used to organize multiple subscriptions and apply policies or settings (like Defender for Cloud) across them.

Subscription:
This is where your actual resources (VMs, storage, etc.) live.

