Note: One important thing, to get full security alerts, deep investigation capabilities, and Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) from a Virtual Machine, you must have the Microsoft Defender for Endpoint agent installed in the VM.

While Defender for Cloud provides agentless scanning for basic malware detection but if you want advance alert for the virtual machine in that case, you have to installed
Microsoft Defender for Endpoint agent.

If your goal is to get basic security alerts from a VM, then you do NOT need to install the Microsoft Defender for Endpoint agent.

“For most Azure services like storage, SQL, and networking, no agent is required because Azure collects logs by default. Agents are mainly needed for virtual machines when we want deeper security insights.

Basically, defender agent is not needed Mostly for Azure services that belong to PaaS.

Because those services are:

Fully managed by Azure
Already integrated with logging and monitoring systems
Continuously sending data to Defender automatically

